## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical TF.js deployment knowledge, including model conversion, quantization trade-offs, and browser inference pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- TensorFlow.js converter usage and quantization options
- Input/output shape alignment between Keras and tfjs graph model
- Static hosting of model.json and shard files
- Client-side preprocessing (224x224, [-1,1]) and top-k decoding

## Code Example
```javascript
// Load and infer with a TF.js GraphModel (illustrative)
const model = await tf.loadGraphModel('/models/mobilenetv2_web/model.json');
function preprocess(img) {
  const t = tf.browser.fromPixels(img).toFloat();
  const resized = tf.image.resizeBilinear(t, [224, 224]);
  const norm = resized.div(tf.scalar(127.5)).sub(tf.scalar(1));
  return norm.expandDims(0);
}
async function infer(img) {
  const input = preprocess(img);
  const logits = model.predict(input);
  const probs = logits.softmax ? logits.softmax() : logits;
  const data = await probs.data();
  const top3 = Array.from(data).map((p, i) => ({i, p}))
    .sort((a, b) => b.p - a.p)
    .slice(0, 3);
  return top3.map(x => x.i);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-model optimizations that preserve SLA and isolate tail latency in a multi-model serving setup.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-model caching for shared embeddings
- Per-model batching with HoLB isolation
- Cache sizing and eviction strategy
- Profiling and latency targeting

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo JS-like sketch; real impl would be in Python with TF Serving hooks
class LRUCache {
  constructor(cap) { this.cap = cap; this.map = new Map(); }
  get(k) { if (!this.map.has(k)) return null; const v = this.map.get(k); this.map.delete(k); this.map.set(k, v); return v; }
  put(k, v) { this.map.set(k, v); if (this.map.size > this.cap) { const first = this.map.keys().next().value; this.map.delete(first); } }
}
```
```python
from collections import OrderedDict
class LRUCache:
    def __init__(self, cap):
        self.cap = cap
        self.store = OrderedDict()
    def get(self, k):
        if k not in self.store: return None
        self.store.move_to_end(k)
        return self.store[k]
    def put(self, k, v):
        self.store[k] = v
        self.store.move_to_end(k)
        if len(self.store) > self.cap:
            self.store.popitem(last=False)
```

